        "comments": "The assembly daGalBore1.hap1.1 is based on 60x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The sample is tetraploid (4n = 44). Hap1 is a chromosome-level curated assembly. The other 3 haplotypes are in HAP2 file and are scaffold-level curated. Some haplotypic inversions in HAP1 were detected on: Chromosome 2 from 13.02 to 15.86, 19.37 to 24.58, 19.37 to 26.24, 31.51 to 34.80 and 35.26 to 38.44 Mbp, Chromosome 9 from 21.86 to 32.90 Mbp and Chromosome 10 from 21.98 to 23.44 Mbp.",
